❓Question
You are given an integer array nums and an integer k.
Find a contiguous subarray whose length is exactly k and which has the maximum average value.
Return the maximum average.

Example
Input:
nums = [1,12,-5,-6,50,3]
k = 4
Output: 12.75000
Explanation:
The subarray is:
[12,-5,-6,50]
Sum:
12 + (-5) + (-6) + 50 = 51
Average:
51 / 4 = 12.75

✅Approach — Fixed Size Sliding Window
Since the subarray length must always be k, use a fixed-size sliding window.
First calculate the sum of the first k elements.
Then slide the window:
[1, 12, -5, -6]  →  [12, -5, -6, 50]
When moving the window:
Remove the element leaving from the left.
Add the new element entering from the right.
So: sum = sum - nums[low] + nums[high];
Keep track of the maximum window sum.
Finally: maximum average = maximum sum / k

Code
class Solution {
    public double findMaxAverage(int[] nums, int k) {
        int sum = 0;
        int res = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int low = 0;
        int high = k - 1;
        // First window
        for (int i = low; i <= high; i++) {
            sum += nums[i];
        }
        while (high < nums.length) {
            res = Math.max(sum, res);
            low++;
            high++;
            if (high >= nums.length) {
                break;
            } else {
                sum -= nums[low - 1];
                sum += nums[high];
            }
        }
        double average = (double) res / k;
        return average;
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
